part-i-p5 : Block
part-i-p5 = prose (cons "Reflection extends this activity to the language's own definitions. Existing languages retain their specified syntax and semantics while their interpreters, checkers, and transformations become operands of further computation. Under the stated evaluator-adequacy and machine-simulation premises, one machine-realized evaluator executes every represented program, including these operations on programs. The chosen native route is through C and a downstream compiler, with the correctness relations composed across that route. Symbolic residuals retain unknown inputs; dependency evidence governs reuse; continuing interactions retain their history; and decentralized exchange makes constructions and their rationales available to other participants. *Hyperactivity* names this conductance of knowledge into further activity: a persistent, interactive language of processes that includes the work of understanding and changing them." nil)
